# Key layout for the H96 Max M9S infrared receiver.
#
# The device name comes from the PWM node the Rockchip IR driver binds to --
# pwm0_2ch_0, at 0x27330000 on RK3576 -- and EventHub turns '.' into '_', so the
# file has to be called exactly 27330000_pwm.kl. Without it Android falls back
# to Generic.kl and the whole remote is inert:
#
#   EventHub: New device: id=1, ... name='27330000.pwm',
#             keyLayout='/product/usr/keylayout/Generic.kl'
#
# The scancode-to-keycode step happens in the kernel, not here: the three
# rockchip,key_table nodes in rk3576-m9s.dts -- ir_key1 for the bundled handset,
# ir_key2 and ir_key6 for the other two usercodes the box answers -- already
# emit Linux keycodes. This file only maps those to Android ones, so the set
# below is what those tables can produce plus the spares stock carried.
#
# Based on stock's vendor/usr/keylayout/27330000_pwm.kl, which is Rockchip's
# generic RBOX layout. Deviations are marked; everything else is unchanged.

key 28    ENTER
key 116   POWER
key 158   BACK
key 139   MENU
key 217   SEARCH
key 141   SETTINGS
key 164   MEDIA_PLAY_PAUSE
key 232   DPAD_CENTER
key 108   DPAD_DOWN
key 103   DPAD_UP
key 102   HOME
key 104   CHANNEL_UP
key 105   DPAD_LEFT
key 106   DPAD_RIGHT
key 109   CHANNEL_DOWN
key 115   VOLUME_UP
key 114   VOLUME_DOWN
key 110   INSERT
key 111   FORWARD_DEL
#key 143   NOTIFICATION
key 64    F6
key 65    F7
key 66    F8
key 67    F9
key 142   POWER
key 143   POWER
key 152   POWER
key 176   SETTINGS
key 177   PAGE_UP
key 178   PAGE_DOWN
key 388   PROFILE_SWITCH
key 92    PAGE_UP
key 93    PAGE_DOWN
key 14    DEL
key 113   VOLUME_MUTE
key 2     1
key 3     2
key 4     3
key 5     4
key 6     5
key 7     6
key 8     7
key 9     8
key 10    9
key 11    0
key 183   SETTINGS
key 184   CALL
#key 185   PROG_YELLOW
key 186   CALCULATOR

key 398   PROG_RED
key 399   PROG_GREEN
key 400   PROG_YELLOW
key 401   PROG_BLUE
key 402   CHANNEL_UP
key 403   CHANNEL_DOWN

# Added. ir_key1 emits KEY_NEXT (407) and KEY_PREVIOUS (412) for the two skip
# buttons on the M9S handset, and stock's layout -- written for a different
# remote -- maps neither, so both did nothing even on stock.
key 407   MEDIA_NEXT
key 412   MEDIA_PREVIOUS

# Deliberately unmapped, both emitted by the dts and neither identifiable from
# it:
#   KEY_A   (30)  from ir_key1
#   KEY_F15 (185) from ir_key2, which stock also left commented out
# An unmapped key does nothing; a wrongly guessed one does the wrong thing.
# Identify them with `adb shell getevent -l /dev/input/event0`, then add them.
